Subject: [PATCH 37/38] page: Fire Emblem Fates helpers: the Helpers heading,
 the True hit row and the enemy-turn help line

Round 80 (docs/ROUND80_PLAN.md A1, build/r80/home/HOME_DESIGN.md; the owner's
pick F-057, run on the standing OK F-059 (3)). The row words are Grok's
(docs/collab/ROUND80_HELPERS_GROK.md).

Storage: a top-level `fates_helpers` field in Zakuro's Settings, written as a
`[fates_helpers]` table in settings.toml (enemy_phase = "normal" | "2x" | "4x",
true_hit = false | true). skip_serializing_if = is_default: at the defaults
nothing is written, so an untouched settings file stays byte for byte what it
was; or_default: a value this build does not know (say "8x") gives the defaults
for the table and keeps every other setting. Not per game (GameSettings): the
"Follow the general settings" button leaves it, has_own() stays false, and
split_for_save keeps it in the shared file, so Fire Emblem Fates and Seal of
Flames share one choice. Never a randomizer row: no seed, answer, run id or
share code changes.

Core: new zakuro-core fates_helpers.rs (plain data: Helpers { enemy_phase,
true_hit }, EnemyPhase Normal / X2 / X4 with factor() 1 / 2 / 4, name(), key()).
System keeps the rows the frontend hands over (set_helpers, at game start in
start_game and on every apply_settings); System::helpers() returns them for
Fire Emblem Fates' title id 0004000000179800 (Seal of Flames shares it) and the
defaults for every other title. The getters the enemy-phase pacing and the
True hit painter read: System::helpers().enemy_phase().factor() and
System::helpers().true_hit(). Nothing here reads or writes guest memory; with
the defaults nothing acts at all.

Paused window: under the Randomizer button, with the same Fates-title gate but
not hidden by rando_blocked, menus::helper_rows draws the heading "Helpers",
"Enemy phase [Normal][2x][4x]", "True hit [Off][On]" (one hover sentence each)
and the help line "The game's own Options line 6 (Off, Move, or All) and the
Start key still skip the enemy turn. These rows do not change that." A change
pushes Action::Settings (save + apply_settings), as the Settings window does.
The Paused window gets .vscroll(true) and a max height of the screen less 16
px, so it scrolls in a short window (800 x 480) instead of running past its
bottom; that is a visible change for every game's Paused window. Its egui id
is set to "Paused" explicitly (the same name it had).

Page robot (FEF_PAGEBOT, headless only): {"esc": "paused"} draws the Helpers
rows into the robot's windowless context and holds the game while open (as the
Esc menu does); their targets are helpers:section,
helpers:opt:enemy_phase=<normal|2x|4x>, helpers:opt:true_hit=<off|on>; a click
that changes a row runs apply_settings (the run's own APPDATA);
{"expect_settings": {...}} reads the [fates_helpers] table back from
settings::path() (now pub). frame() stays for the tests; the program calls
frame_with.

Tests (cargo test --lib): settings U1 untouched_settings_write_no_helpers_table,
U2 helpers_round_trip, U3 a_bad_helper_value_keeps_the_rest, U4
an_older_file_has_the_default_helpers, U5
follow_the_general_settings_leaves_the_helpers; game_pick U6
seal_and_fates_share_the_helpers; menus U7 helper_rows_show_only_for_fates, U8
clicking_true_hit_saves, U9 the_paused_window_fits_a_short_screen (800 x 480 and
800 x 360, Fates and another game), the_helper_words_say_what_the_plan_asks;
pagebot the_robot_sets_the_helpers_and_reads_them_back; core fates_helpers
the_defaults_are_todays_game, the_factors_and_words. zakuro 130 passed,
zakuro-core 232, zakuro-fs 23.

Round 80 repair (B2, 2026-11-25), the plan's cut 3: robot proof E2 found
that 2x / 4x pacing (the former patch 0038, not in the series any more)
could not reach the plan's time goal (4x took 0.82 of Normal's time, 2x
0.88) while every fight and turn banner stays at normal speed. So the
Paused window has no Enemy phase row: menus::helper_rows draws the heading,
